-2.1 **Content idempotents are central.** For fixed $\alpha$ the set $I_\alpha$ is the set of all orderings of one multiset of entries of $I$ of size $d$, hence a single orbit of the position permutation action of $S_d$ on $I^d$; it is finite. The element $e_\alpha=\sum_{i\in I_\alpha}e(i)$ is therefore the symmetrization over that orbit of the monomial $\prod_{r=1}^{d}E_{i_r}(x_r)$: permuting the variables $x_1,\dots,x_d$ permutes the orderings in $I_\alpha$, so $e_\alpha$ is a symmetric polynomial in $x_1,\dots,x_d$. [step 1.1, given, algebra]
